WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.065
Identity design determines who or what is allowed to read data and take action.

2
00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:15.654
AI systems may involve user identities, service identities, application identities, delegated access, shared service accounts, API keys, tokens, and secrets.

3
00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:20.335
Those identities should not be blended into one vague permission layer.

4
00:00:20.335 --> 00:00:28.009
A model request, a user request, an application call, and a downstream API action may all involve different authority.

5
00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:36.911
Least privilege means each user, service, tool, and integration receives only the permissions needed for its intended task and context.

6
00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:40.824
A document lookup tool does not need write access to tickets.

7
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:45.582
A summarization workflow does not need cloud administrator privileges.

8
00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:51.260
A model should not receive every available tool by default just because the tools exist.

9
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.860
Narrow permissions reduce the damage from mistakes, prompt manipulation, and implementation bugs.

10
00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.694
Per-user authorization and tenant boundaries are especially important.

11
00:01:02.694 --> 00:01:10.445
If a user cannot access a document or customer record directly, the AI system should not retrieve it for them indirectly.

12
00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:17.351
If one tenant's data is indexed in a vector store, another tenant's prompt should not be able to retrieve it.

13
00:01:17.351 --> 00:01:25.178
Authorization should happen before sensitive content enters the model context, not after the model has already seen it.

14
00:01:25.178 --> 00:01:28.555
The model should not be able to expand its own access.

15
00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:37.379
Actions should be authorized by application code, identity systems, policy engines, or downstream services, not by model confidence.

16
00:01:37.379 --> 00:01:41.600
Approval workflows should be explicit for high-impact actions.

17
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.588
Secrets and tokens should be protected from prompts, logs, and tool outputs.

18
00:01:46.588 --> 00:01:52.803
AI architecture is safer when permissions are deterministic and reviewable outside the model.
